WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:09.260
In Avengers: Infinity War, the evil
villain Thanos likely draw inspiration

00:00:09.269 --> 00:00:13.100
from Malthus. Like Thanos, Malthus was
convinced that population growth would

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:16.109
outpace growth in living standards, leading
to disaster.

00:00:16.109 --> 00:00:19.890
Unlike Thanos, Malthus did not use a
magic glove to kill half the universe.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:24.420
But Thanos and Malthus are wrong. As
technology improves, so does efficiency.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.779
Earth's population has grown
significantly over the centuries, but

00:00:27.779 --> 00:00:31.710
calories are more available, and extreme
poverty more scarce, than ever before.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:35.399
The key reason? Efficiency and
productivity gains, and innovation, allow

00:00:35.399 --> 00:00:39.239
living standards to grow faster than the
population. Instead of delivering death

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:41.550
and destruction,
Thanos should focus on increasing

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:45.600
productivity, innovation, and efficiency.
Specifically, he should encourage rule of

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.489
law, strong liberal institutions, and an
entrepreneurial culture. Break down trade

00:00:50.489 --> 00:00:54.750
barriers between planets and galaxies.
Deregulate businesses. Lower the

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.590
corporate tax rate on each and every
planet. Patent reform! And, of course,

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:03.000
generous funding for scientific research.
Here's hoping the Avengers stop Thanos

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.860
in the next film. They are on the side of
the best social and economic analysis.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:12.000
The internet tells me that some of you
think Thanos did nothing wrong. Why? Let us

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.930
know in your comments. Also, let us know
what other topics you'd like our

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:20.070
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be
sure to LIKE and subscribe for more

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:23.720
research and videos from AEI.

